# headon-fight: two bodies of one footprint meet head on in a lane one body wide, on attack-move orders.
# On move legs allies swap places at once; a fight or patrol leg takes no swap (its facing serves its weapons), and
# the hold has no other way out of this meet, so the two stood for good with their orders. Once both stand dead
# 600 ticks (nothing either waits on has made progress) the swap serves them too: the late swap.
# The lane lies inside one routing sector, so no passage admission keeps the two apart.
# Keys: g.L.arrived, g.R.arrived (1 each; 0 before), work.late_swaps.total.
scn 1
name headon-fight
ticks 2400
seed 7
players 1
weapons off
map flat 32 32
wall 0 0 32 14
wall 0 16 32 16
type m mover 2 2500 10 1.79999
group L 0 m 1 cells 2,14
group R 0 m 1 cells 28,14
at 2 fight L 27 15
at 2 fight R 5 15
